1. What you may do
   You may download, install and use the Archipel desktop app (the "Software") from this
   repository, for yourself or for the organisation you work for.
   - Free use: one landscape with up to 50 applications and places, at no cost.
   - Larger use needs a paid licence key, bought from inside the app. The terms shown at purchase
     apply to that licence.

2. What you may not do
   - copy, change, translate or build on the Software, other than installing it;
   - redistribute, sell, rent, lend or sublicense the Software, or offer it as a service to others;
   - reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except where the law allows it
     regardless of this clause;
   - remove or work around the licence check, or remove notices of ownership.

3. Your data
   Your workspace (the folder with your landscapes and settings) is yours. The Software reads and
   writes it on your computer and in the git repository you choose. The licence check sends only
   the licence key and an identifier of the workspace to the licence provider.

4. No warranty
   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Keep a copy of your workspace
   (for example in git).

5. Liability
   To the extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any damage that results from using
   the Software, including loss of data or profit.

6. Ending
   This licence ends when you break it. You then stop using the Software and remove it.

7. Law
   Dutch law applies. Disputes go to the competent court in the Netherlands.

